intermountain healthcare the sponsors of  this next segment support a very special  organization that gives our local kids  happy feet here's how  [Music]  hi i'm christina kober with under  mountain healthcare we're here today  with the goody two shoes foundation i'm  here with nikki bertie the ceo of goody2  shoes uh enter mountain recently had the  opportunity to sponsor one of the local  shoe distribution events so nikki if you  want to tell us a little bit about the  event about goody two-shoes foundation  sure i'd love to and we're super  appreciative of the support that you  guys have provided goody two shoes has  been outfitting children in need here in  clark county since 2003 we have  outfitted over a hundred and seventeen  thousand kids uh through the years of  doing shoe distributions we have a 48  foot mobile unit that we take to schools  we go to a different title one tier one  pre-scheduled school almost every week  we pull ups like a giant transformer  we have racks that come out and set up  and and  doors that open and then the kids are  pre-selected based on me we outfit about  120 to 150 kids every 30 minutes  one-on-one with a community volunteer  who takes them through to make sure it's  a properly fitting pair of shoes but the  crux of goody two-shoes programming is  to give the kids the opportunity to  select their very own brand new pair of  sneakers so they do that the volunteer  makes sure the shoes fit we also give  them six pairs of socks because years  ago we saw the kids didn't have socks as  well and then they'll check out we  double check to make sure it's a  properly fitting pair of sneakers they  check out so we do inventory control  they grab a dental kit because we saw a  lot of tooth issues going on  over the years and then they head back  to class a lot of people oftentimes  don't think about the need for shoes  and for families that are in dire  straits or lower socioeconomic  background  shoes are often something foregone to  rent or groceries and so it's really  important that kids have the proper  footwear to be able to go to school and  actively participate um  bad shoes shoes with holes duct taped  whatever can become a really big flash  point for bullying and ridicule and so  we want to make sure that we're boosting  self-confidence we're getting kids in a  properly fitting pair of sneakers so  they can actively be involved in the  school environment and they're not  thinking about shoes that are too small  or too big on their feet that they're  focused in the classroom for myself and  for my other fellow caregivers to be at  the shoe distribution event it was very  meaningful  we get to see an immediate impact take  away we got to see  the at the lights go into kids eyes when  they got to pick out a pair of shoes a  brand new pair of shoes for the first  time and so this was really meaningful  work and it just left a lasting  feel-good moment for many of our  caregivers to be able to volunteer and  see  some of the resources going to use in  this way volunteers are critical to the  work that goody two-shoes does we only  have a staff of four and so everything  that happens out in the community at  every school we visit is the  responsibility and the result of  volunteers stepping up to make a  difference in our community it's a  simple four hour commitment usually on a  friday morning at a different title one  tier one school there's great  opportunities to come out see the impact  such as your team did and come out and  make a difference and see those smiles  and see those shining eyes and those  happy faces and dancing feet  such a great organization thank you  intermountain healthcare for sponsoring  that segment for more information visit  goody2shoes.org  [Music]
 

